  'leaf_yellowing_pattern IS NOT NULL', 'dsl-1.0', 'EVENT', FALSE, NULL,
  'Run the diagnosis sequence before recommending anything. Step 1: is the soil near the root wet? Step 2: dig one sample plant. Step 3: which leaves are yellow — old or new? Step 4: check the last three days for temperatures above 35 C. Do NOT recommend urea on the yellowing signal alone.',
  'पिवळी पाने दिसल्यावर पहिली कृती युरिया नाही — निदान आहे. १) मुळाजवळची माती ओली आहे का. २) एक नमुना रोप उकरून पहा. ३) कोणती पाने पिवळी — जुनी की नवी. ४) गेल्या तीन दिवसांत ३५ अंशांवर तापमान गेले का. जुनी पाने पिवळी म्हणजे नत्र; नवी पाने पिवळी म्हणजे लोह किंवा जस्त.',
  'Six distinct causes produce similar yellowing and the treatments differ. Two of them are made worse by the reflexive response. Nitrogen applied to waterlogged soil worsens the condition; nitrogen applied to lime-induced iron lock-up does nothing except grow foliage at the rhizome''s expense.',
  'Prevents wasted input cost and, more importantly, prevents a missed rot diagnosis worth up to u = 0.70.',
  0.9, 'A', 'DERIVED', NULL, 'partial',
  'This is the most frequently triggered diagnostic rule in the whole knowledge base for this belt, because calcareous yellowing here is expected rather than exceptional. One line of guidance — old leaves means nitrogen, new leaves means micronutrients — saves fertiliser cost every season.');

