  'Land preparation phase',
  'पूर्वमशागतीचा टप्पा',
  NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, NULL,
  'Physically remove perennial weed tubers and rhizomes — nutsedge, bermuda grass and similar — along with stones. Do not rely on later weeding to control them.',
  'लव्हाळा, हराळी, कुंदा यांसारख्या बहुवार्षिक तणांचे कंद व काश्या वेचून काढा, तसेच मोठे दगड-गोटे. नंतरच्या खुरपणीवर विसंबून राहू नये.',
  'Ginger emerges slowly and cannot outcompete established perennial weeds. More importantly, heavy later weeding injures the rhizome, and Pythium and Fusarium enter through those wounds.',
  'Acts through the disease pathway rather than through competition alone.',
  0.85, 'A', 'SRC-D', NULL, 'none',
  'The causal chain runs: heavy FYM carries weed seed, weed pressure forces more weeding, weeding injures the rhizome, injury admits rot. Weed removal two months before planting is therefore a disease-prevention operation, not a tidiness one.');

