  'Pre-season planning AND water_available_oct_feb_litres is unknown or less than requirement',
  'हंगामापूर्व नियोजन, ऑक्टोबर-फेब्रुवारीची पाणी उपलब्धता माहीत नाही किंवा अपुरी आहे',
  'water_available_oct_feb_litres IS NULL OR water_available_oct_feb_litres < seasonal_water_requirement_litres', 'dsl-1.0', 'ONCE_UNTIL_RESOLVED', FALSE, NULL,
  'Assess water source capacity before anything else. Compute the October to February requirement for THIS plot from its own soil texture, the local evaporation record and the measured drip efficiency — do not use a single universal figure. About 27 lakh litres per acre is an illustrative mid-case for heavy soil under efficient drip; lighter soil, hotter conditions or lower system efficiency raise it. If supply is inadequate, reduce area rather than reduce water per acre.',
  'लागवडीपूर्वी पाण्याच्या स्रोताची क्षमता तपासा. ऑक्टोबर ते फेब्रुवारीची गरज या शेतासाठी स्वतंत्रपणे काढा — त्याच्या मातीचा प्रकार, स्थानिक बाष्पीभवनाची नोंद आणि ठिबकाची प्रत्यक्ष कार्यक्षमता यावरून. एकच सार्वत्रिक आकडा वापरू नका. एकरी सुमारे २७ लाख लिटर हा भारी जमिनीत कार्यक्षम ठिबकासाठीचा उदाहरणादाखल मध्यम अंदाज आहे; हलकी जमीन, जास्त उष्णता किंवा कमी कार्यक्षमता असल्यास तो वाढतो. पाणी अपुरे असल्यास क्षेत्र कमी करा — प्रति एकर पाणी कमी करू नका.',
  'Rain ends in early October but crop demand peaks in October and November at 22,000 and 20,000 litres per acre per day. The entire late-season load falls on stored or pumped water at exactly the time the water table is falling. EXPERT AMENDMENT: the 27 lakh litre figure is illustrative, not universal. It must be computed per plot from soil texture, local evaporation and measured drip efficiency.',
  'Water exhaustion during G4 carries u = 0.20 to 0.40, and because seed cost is already sunk the financial loss is close to total rather than proportional.',
  0.8, 'A', 'DERIVED', 0.3, 'none',
  '55 percent of years here fall below the long-term average rainfall, so this assessment must be run on a poor-year assumption rather than an average one. A farm pond carries 50 percent subsidy and solves this alongside the monsoon drainage problem — see Domain 10.');

