  'calibration_done IS FALSE', 'dsl-1.0', 'ONCE_UNTIL_RESOLVED', FALSE, NULL,
  'Mark all moisture-derived advisory LOW CONFIDENCE and disable automated irrigation triggers. Fall back to the month-wise table plus rain deduction. Tell the user this is happening and why.',
  'calibration झालेले नसल्यास ओलावा-आधारित सल्ला कमी विश्वासार्ह म्हणून दाखवा आणि स्वयंचलित ठिबक बंद ठेवा. तक्ता आणि पाऊस वजावट यावर चालवा — आणि हे वापरकर्त्याला सांगा.',
  'Capacitive sensors respond to bulk dielectric permittivity, which varies strongly with clay content, so factory calibration is invalid on vertisol. Two-point calibration using plot soil is required.',
  'None if the fallback is used. Significant if uncalibrated readings drive irrigation.',
  0.85, 'B', 'SRC-D', NULL, 'full',
  'Calibration needs one handful of plot soil, a container and a day. Saturation detection works even without it, because recognising very wet is qualitative, so the red alert survives while the deficit thresholds do not.');

