  'Nutrient planning initiated',
  'अन्नद्रव्य नियोजन सुरू',
  NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, NULL,
  'Set potassium, not nitrogen, as the governing nutrient. Measured uptake is about 59 kg K per acre against 49 kg N and 17 kg P.',
  'पालाश हेच अद्रकाचे प्रमुख अन्नद्रव्य आहे, नत्र नाही. प्रत्यक्ष उचल एकरी सुमारे ५९ किलो पालाश, ४९ किलो नत्र आणि १७ किलो स्फुरद अशी मोजली गेली आहे.',
  'Potassium uptake exceeds nitrogen uptake in measured data, and potassium leaves the field inside the harvested rhizome while most nitrogen remains in foliage that returns to the soil. So potassium is both the largest uptake and the largest net export.',
  'Sets the priority order for the whole domain. Under-replacement of potassium is the most common and most correctable nutritional error in this crop.',
  0.85, 'A', 'SRC-Q', NULL, 'full',
  'This inverts the habitual assumption that nitrogen is the main fertiliser. Nitrogen shows its effect visibly in green foliage; potassium shows its effect underground where nobody looks until harvest.');

ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

  'Dose setting AND soil_test_available is false',
  'खत मात्रा ठरवायची आहे पण माती परीक्षण उपलब्ध नाही',
  NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, NULL,
  'Use the safe starting range: 40 to 48 kg N, 20 to 30 kg P, 40 to 60 kg K per acre. Keep nitrogen at the lower end and potassium at the upper end. Mark confidence MEDIUM and tell the user a soil test would sharpen this.',
  'सुरक्षित प्रारंभ श्रेणी वापरा — एकरी नत्र ४० ते ४८ किलो, स्फुरद २० ते ३० किलो, पालाश ४० ते ६० किलो. नत्र खालच्या टोकाला, पालाश वरच्या टोकाला ठेवा. माती परीक्षण केल्यास मात्रा अचूक करता येईल.',
  'State recommendations range from 28 to 51 kg N per acre. The highest uptake in semi-arid conditions was recorded at a lower nitrogen dose, and Kannad is semi-arid. The Mahima-specific trial also points to less phosphorus and more potassium, which suits calcareous soil where phosphorus is fixed.',
  'Both extremes are documented as harmful — deficiency limits yield, and indiscriminate use degrades soil physical, chemical and biological condition and reduces yield significantly.',
  0.78, 'A', 'DERIVED', NULL, 'full',
  'The engine gives fertiliser advice from day one rather than refusing until a soil test exists. It says the advice is generic and says why, which is different from pretending to precision it does not have.');

