  'dap BETWEEN 108 AND 115 AND k_late_split_1_date IS NULL', 'dsl-1.0', 'WINDOW', FALSE, NULL,
  'Apply about 15 kg K per acre. Explain clearly why: the crop looks healthy now, but the rhizome is filling right now and it fills on potassium.',
  'पालाशाचा हप्ता द्या — एकरी सुमारे १५ किलो. पीक चांगले दिसत असले तरी गड्डा नेमका आत्ता भरतो आहे, आणि तो पालाशावर भरतो. हा हप्ता वगळू नये.',
  'The Maharashtra schedule adds two potassium splits after nitrogen has finished, bringing the season total to about 60 kg per acre which closely matches the measured uptake of about 59 kg. Without these splits the schedule under-supplies the nutrient the crop removes most.',
  'u = 0.12 estimated for skipping the late potassium splits.',
  0.8, 'A', 'SRC-Q', 0.12, 'none',
  'This is the most commonly skipped operation in the entire schedule, and the reason is psychological rather than agronomic. By 110 DAP the crop is green and vigorous and the fertiliser work feels finished.');

