  'Seed treatment is being planned',
  'बेणे प्रक्रिया ठरवली जात आहे',
  NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, NULL,
  'Treat seed rhizome twice — once before storage and again before planting. Hot water at 51 C for 10 minutes followed by Trichoderma harzianum at 15 g per kg gave the best result among biological treatments. Then shade dry before any further biological step.',
  'बेणे प्रक्रिया दोन वेळा करा — साठवणीपूर्वी आणि लागवडीपूर्वी. ५१ अंश सेल्सिअस पाण्यात दहा मिनिटे, नंतर ट्रायकोडर्मा हार्जियानम प्रति किलो पंधरा ग्रॅम. मग सावलीत सुकवूनच पुढील जैविक प्रक्रिया करा.',
  'Seed rhizome is the primary entry route for both soft rot and bacterial wilt, and once the pathogen is in the soil it cannot be removed. Recorded germination was 80 to 83 percent untreated against 93 to 98 percent treated. Treating only before planting does not address infection already established inside the rhizome during storage.',
  'u = 0.135 on establishment alone. On roughly 800 kg of seed a 15 percent germination difference is worth about 120 to 150 kg of seed. The disease prevention value is separate and larger.',
  0.85, 'A', 'SRC-Q', 0.135, 'none',
  'The twice-treated instruction is easy to lose. Seed goes into storage in December and comes out in May, and the December step is the one that gets skipped because the crop is not on anyone''s mind then.');

