  '(fog_observed IS TRUE AND MONTH IN [DEC, JAN, FEB]) OR (saturation_hours > 12 AND MONTH IN [JUL, AUG, SEP])', 'dsl-1.0', 'SILENT_GUARD', FALSE, NULL,
  'Treat July to September as the soil-borne season driven by saturation, and December to February as the foliar season driven by fog. Different triggers, different responses, different times of year.',
  'जुलै ते सप्टेंबर हा जमिनीखालील रोगांचा हंगाम — कारण संपृक्तता. डिसेंबर ते फेब्रुवारी हा पानांवरील रोगांचा हंगाम — कारण धुके. वेगळे संकेत, वेगळे उपाय, वेगळा काळ.',
  'Soft rot peaks in August and September with high humidity and saturation, while leaf spot and blotch follow prolonged fog in winter. Conflating them would apply the wrong trigger at the wrong time of year.',
  'Ensures the correct protocol fires in each season.',
  0.8, 'A', 'DERIVED', NULL, 'full',
  'The fog rule says to spray until the crop is seven months old, which from a late May planting reaches December or January — exactly the winter fog period here. The published rule and the local calendar align, so it is a real trigger rather than a theoretical one.');

