  'MONTH IN [JUL, AUG, SEP] AND exposed_rhizomes_observed IS TRUE', 'dsl-1.0', 'EVENT', FALSE, NULL,
  'Cover exposed rhizomes with soil immediately, without waiting for the scheduled earthing up. Rhizome fly larvae enter through exposed rhizomes.',
  'उघडे पडलेले गड्डे तात्काळ मातीने झाकून घ्या — ठरलेल्या उटाळणीची वाट पाहू नका. कंदमाशीच्या अळ्या उघड्या गड्ड्यांमधून आत शिरतात.',
  'The source gives the explicit instruction to cover exposed rhizomes during July to September, which is the rhizome fly peak. Rhizome expansion and rainfall both push soil away from the crown, so exposure recurs between earthing operations.',
  'Blocks the entry event for a pest carrying 0.175 that also opens the rot pathway.',
  0.88, 'A', 'SRC-Q', NULL, 'partial',
  'This is a standing instruction rather than a scheduled operation, which is why it needs its own rule rather than being folded into earthing up. Exposure happens between the two scheduled earthings.');

