  'Market selection for a consignment',
  'माल कोणत्या बाजारात न्यायचा हे ठरवायचे आहे',
  NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, NULL,
  'Split the consignment rather than choosing one market. Send 20 to 30 percent of the best grade to a small or local market where arrivals are low and prices higher, 50 to 60 percent to a large market that can absorb volume, and consider processing the lowest 10 to 20 percent instead of selling it.',
  'एकच बाजार निवडण्याऐवजी माल विभागून पाठवा. सर्वोत्तम प्रतीचा २० ते ३०% भाग लहान किंवा स्थानिक बाजारात — तिथे आवक कमी आणि भाव जास्त. ५० ते ६०% मोठ्या बाजारात — तो मोठे प्रमाण शोषतो. आणि खालच्या प्रतीचा १० ते २०% भाग विकण्याऐवजी सुंठ करण्याचा विचार करा.',
  'Chandrapur took the highest price of the day on an arrival of 8 to 25 quintal, while Mumbai handled 884 to 1,556 quintal at a lower range. Small arrivals command higher prices but a small market cannot absorb a large consignment — sending it all there would collapse the price.',
  'Pure price capture. Costs transport planning.',
  0.72, 'B', 'DERIVED', NULL, 'full',
  'Transport cost has not been measured and it decides whether the split is worth making. Mumbai is roughly 350 km and Nagpur roughly 500 km from here, so the freight on a 10 tonne load is material.');

