  NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, NULL,
  'Ask older growers and seed sellers in the district. Aurangabad appears as a ginger district in two of three published lists and a landrace called Aurangabadi is separately recorded, so local tradition is probably deeper than assumed.',
  'जिल्ह्यातील जुन्या शेतकऱ्यांकडे आणि बेणे विक्रेत्यांकडे चौकशी करा. तीनपैकी दोन यादींमध्ये औरंगाबाद अद्रक जिल्हा म्हणून नोंदवलेला आहे, आणि ''औरंगाबादी'' नावाची स्थानिक जातही स्वतंत्रपणे नोंदवलेली आहे — म्हणजे इथली परंपरा वाटते त्यापेक्षा जुनी असावी.',
  'Two independent signals point the same way. A place-named landrace usually indicates sustained local cultivation over a long period, and that means adapted material and accumulated practical knowledge may exist locally.',
  'Could surface a locally adapted variety and practical knowledge that no publication contains.',
  0.65, 'B', 'SRC-D', NULL, 'full',
  'This was an unexpected finding. The working assumption was that ginger is new to this district; two source lists and a landrace name suggest otherwise, which changes who is worth asking.');

